{"id": "whnahanni", "name": "Nahanni National Park Reserve", "short": "Nahanni", "place": "Northwest Territories, Canada", "lat": 61.5, "lon": -125.5, "side": "l", "cont": "North America", "country": "Canada", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Wolves, grizzlies and Dall sheep above a wild boreal river canyon.", "tip": {"id": "hare", "title": "Crash the snowshoe hares", "text": "Set Snowshoe hare to -100% and watch the lynx lose their main prey, while foxes, black bears and wolves lean harder on other foods."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Nahanni National Park Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nahanni_National_Park_Reserve"}, {"title": "Parks Canada: Nahanni National Park Reserve", "url": "https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/nt/nahanni/nature"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Dall sheep", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dall_sheep"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Boreal forest of Canada", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boreal_forest_of_Canada"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Nahanni National Park Reserve", "icon": "wolf", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "summer sunlight", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Long northern summer days power a short, intense growing season for the plants of the valley and the alpine slopes."}, {"id": "water", "sp": "south nahanni river and meltwater", "xh": 0.37}, {"id": "fire", "sp": "wildfire", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "Fire is a normal part of boreal forest. It recycles nutrients and opens ground for shrubs and berries."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "soil and limestone minerals", "xh": 0.82}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.94, "desc": "Break down dead plants and animals, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "willow", "sp": "salix glauca", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "A common shrub willow of the reserve, browsed by moose, hares and Dall sheep and used by beavers."}, {"id": "spruce", "sp": "picea glauca", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A main tree of the boreal forest in the valleys. Snowshoe hares gnaw its twigs and bark in winter.", "ic": "willow"}, {"id": "cowberry", "sp": "vaccinium vitis-idaea", "xh": 0.48, "desc": "A low evergreen berry shrub. Its fruit is eaten by bears and foxes, and caribou eat the plant."}, {"id": "sedge", "sp": "carex concinna", "xh": 0.66}, {"id": "lichen", "sp": "cladonia rangiferina", "xh": 0.85, "desc": "Pale ground lichens that are winter food for caribou and, where the ground is bare of snow, Dall sheep."}, {"id": "moose", "sp": "alces alces", "xh": 0.06, "desc": "A big browser of willow and other shrubs. Its carcasses feed wolves, bears and scavengers."}, {"id": "sheep", "sp": "ovis dalli", "xh": 0.22, "desc": "Lives on steep alpine slopes, eating grasses, sedges and willow, and lichens in winter. Wolves, bears and golden eagles prey on it."}, {"id": "caribou", "sp": "rangifer tarandus", "xh": 0.38, "name": "Woodland caribou", "desc": "Eats lichens, plus plants such as cowberry. The reserve is thought to hold two herds, a species at risk in Canada."}, {"id": "hare", "sp": "lepus americanus", "xh": 0.54, "wiki": "Snowshoe hare", "desc": "Eats willow and other woody twigs in winter and is the main prey of lynx. A key food link in the boreal forest.", "ic": "vole"}, {"id": "gsq", "sp": "urocitellus parryii", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "A burrowing squirrel of open tundra and meadows that eats sedges and other plants. Eagles and bears hunt it."}, {"id": "beaver", "sp": "castor canadensis", "xh": 0.88, "wiki": "North American beaver", "desc": "Cuts willow and other woody plants and dams streams, making ponds.", "badge": "Ecosystem engineer"}, {"id": "lynx", "sp": "lynx canadensis", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "A cat that specialises in snowshoe hares and is listed among the mammals of the reserve."}, {"id": "fox", "sp": 